# Valgrind suppressions for the Wayland harness's memcheck runs
# (README.md, "Sanitizers and soak").  Each entry names a report that
# is not the backend's, with the reason it is safe: the garbage
# collector's stack scan, and library internals.  Nothing reached
# through src/wayland*.c is suppressed.

# Emacs's conservative garbage collector scans the C stack and compares
# every word against its heaps, uninitialized words included (etc/DEBUG,
# "Running Emacs under Valgrind").  Without --enable-checking, alloc.c
# does not mark those words defined (USE_VALGRIND).
{
   emacs-gc-conservative-scan-cond
   Memcheck:Cond
   ...
   fun:garbage_collect
}
{
   emacs-gc-conservative-scan-value8
   Memcheck:Value8
   ...
   fun:garbage_collect
}
